{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00268",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.51,
      "end_seconds": 3.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Excuse me, doctor, should I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 3.7,
      "end_seconds": 6.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Right on time. Sit, please. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.4,
      "end_seconds": 11.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "It's a very sore throat, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.79,
      "end_seconds": 15.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.35,
      "end_seconds": 19.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "It's been about two weeks, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.32,
      "end_seconds": 27.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.1,
      "end_seconds": 37.84,
      "duration_seconds": 9.74,
      "text": "Only warm salt water, and it's not much. I'd give it a eight, out of ten. I notice it more with swallowing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.56,
      "end_seconds": 41.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "What about pain on swallowing, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.13,
      "end_seconds": 43.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Yes, for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.6,
      "end_seconds": 46.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.97,
      "end_seconds": 51.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "It happens a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.1,
      "end_seconds": 68.55,
      "duration_seconds": 16.45,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.06,
      "end_seconds": 70.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.3,
      "end_seconds": 72.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Any cough or ear pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.97,
      "end_seconds": 77.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "No cough or ear pain, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.89,
      "end_seconds": 79.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Has there been any rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.75,
      "end_seconds": 84.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "No, uh, I haven't had any rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.83,
      "end_seconds": 97.19,
      "duration_seconds": 12.36,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.62,
      "end_seconds": 100.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.82,
      "end_seconds": 104.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.04,
      "end_seconds": 108.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Well, it's paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.3,
      "end_seconds": 109.0,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.48,
      "end_seconds": 113.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.58,
      "end_seconds": 115.34,
      "duration_seconds": 0.76,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.86,
      "end_seconds": 133.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.16,
      "end_seconds": 136.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.4,
      "end_seconds": 139.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.68,
      "end_seconds": 143.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.44,
      "end_seconds": 148.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.11,
      "end_seconds": 151.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.04,
      "end_seconds": 155.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Okay, I'll just check what's already recorded here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.55,
      "end_seconds": 157.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.19,
      "end_seconds": 170.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.15,
      "end_seconds": 179.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.55,
      "end_seconds": 209.19,
      "duration_seconds": 16.64,
      "text": "Okay: weight 83 kilos, BMI works out to 31.2. And temp 38.9 degrees, height 163 centimetres, respiratory rate 21, pulse is 106 beats a minute, SpO2 95 percent on room air, pressure 121 over 78. Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.51,
      "end_seconds": 211.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.2,
      "end_seconds": 214.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "One moment, I'm updating your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.96,
      "end_seconds": 239.16,
      "duration_seconds": 13.2,
      "text": "Okay, continuing. So, based on your history, my working impression is tonsillitis, probably bacterial. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a very sore throat for about two weeks, and no cough or rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.6,
      "end_seconds": 240.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.81,
      "end_seconds": 244.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.41,
      "end_seconds": 246.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.52,
      "end_seconds": 284.24,
      "duration_seconds": 25.72,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. I'm going to order a throat swab, for sore throat. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'd like you to take amoxicillin, 500 milligrams, three times a day, for five days. You take it by mouth. That should help with throat infection. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.65,
      "end_seconds": 286.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.94,
      "end_seconds": 306.66,
      "duration_seconds": 18.72,
      "text": "Finish the whole course of antibiotics even if you feel better after two days. Gargle with warm salt water a few times a day, it does soothe it. Keep an eye out, and if you can't swallow your saliva or you have trouble breathing, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.19,
      "end_seconds": 308.89,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.65,
      "end_seconds": 312.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Please come and see me in a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.82,
      "end_seconds": 313.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.6,
      "end_seconds": 320.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.05,
      "end_seconds": 328.86,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "So, I take the amoxicillin, 500 milligrams, three times a day and come back in a week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.72,
      "end_seconds": 335.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Call the clinic if you need us in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.83,
      "end_seconds": 338.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Okay, so no questions. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}